'''Treasure Island''' (Japanese: '''たから島''' ''Treasure Island'') is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive island in the [[Alola]] [[region]]. It is located near [[Melemele Island]] and is {{wp|Uninhabited island|uninhabited}} by [[human]]s; however, it is home to many [[wild Pokémon]].

Treasure Island was visited by {{Ash}} and his {{AP|Pikachu}} in ''[[SM020|Partner Promises!]]'' following the recommendation of a saleswoman, who mentions that the island is full of wild Pokémon as well as materials to help make accessories for her shop. Ash and Pikachu spend most of the day there, where they played with the local Pokémon and helped a {{p|Wimpod}} that was lost and separated from its group. It was also where they spotted the [[Guardian deities|spirit guardian]] of [[Akala Island]], {{DL|Guardian deities (anime)|Tapu Lele}}, for the first time.

It appeared in a flashback in ''[[SM031|The Island Whisperer!]]'', when Ash remembered seeing {{p|Tapu Lele}}.

It reappeared in ''[[SM102|Alola, Alola!]]'', when Ash took {{ashcl}} there along with {{an|Misty}}, who was visiting the [[region]], while riding on some [[Poké Ride]] {{p|Mantine}}.

